WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.201 --> 00:00:03.402
-The president is facing
three more days

00:00:03.402 --> 00:00:05.638
of impeachment hearings
this week after a second day

00:00:05.638 --> 00:00:07.673
of damning testimony
and yet another conviction

00:00:07.673 --> 00:00:09.775
of one of his associates.

00:00:09.775 --> 00:00:11.644
For more on this,
it's time for "A Closer Look."

00:00:11.644 --> 00:00:15.447
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:15.447 --> 00:00:18.384
Now, if you've been following
the impeachment hearings,

00:00:18.384 --> 00:00:19.819
I know what
you've been thinking.

00:00:19.819 --> 00:00:23.088
Where...is...the...evidence?

00:00:23.088 --> 00:00:25.024
I mean, only six
of the president's

00:00:25.024 --> 00:00:26.992
closest aides and associates
have been convicted

00:00:26.992 --> 00:00:28.762
or pled guilty to crimes.

00:00:28.762 --> 00:00:32.031
I mean, who among us doesn't
have at least six work friends

00:00:32.031 --> 00:00:34.567
who are also criminals?

00:00:34.567 --> 00:00:37.070
I mean, we all know
every friend group has a Carrie,

00:00:37.070 --> 00:00:38.605
a Miranda, a Charlotte,

00:00:38.605 --> 00:00:43.309
and a Roger who looks like Mary
Poppins' coked-up ex-boyfriend.

00:00:43.309 --> 00:00:45.912
That, of course, is Roger Stone,
a long-time associate

00:00:45.912 --> 00:00:49.081
of President Trump in his actual
outfit from the inauguration.

00:00:49.081 --> 00:00:51.417
And on Friday,
Stone opened his magic umbrella

00:00:51.417 --> 00:00:53.686
and teleported himself to jail.

00:00:53.686 --> 00:00:56.923
-Roger Stone, the
self-proclaimed dirty trickster

00:00:56.923 --> 00:01:01.060
and long-time associate of
President Donald Trump, an ally,

00:01:01.060 --> 00:01:03.396
was found guilty
in federal court

00:01:03.396 --> 00:01:05.965
of witness tampering
and lying to Congress

00:01:05.965 --> 00:01:08.835
about his pursuit
of Russian hacked e-mails

00:01:08.835 --> 00:01:11.938
damaging to Hillary Clinton's
2016 election bid.

00:01:11.938 --> 00:01:14.374
-Man, who could have guessed
this guy was a criminal?

00:01:14.374 --> 00:01:15.608
[ Laughter ]

00:01:15.608 --> 00:01:16.709
I mean, he looks like
a character

00:01:16.709 --> 00:01:19.212
from the 1960s
Adam West "Batman."

00:01:19.212 --> 00:01:21.614
[ Laughter ]

00:01:21.614 --> 00:01:24.550
When they closed the door
of his jail cell,

00:01:24.550 --> 00:01:28.254
it'll go, "Wham! Clink! Pow!"

00:01:28.254 --> 00:01:30.589
Stone is now at least
the sixth Trump associate

00:01:30.589 --> 00:01:33.626
who's been convicted of
or pled guilty to a crime,

00:01:33.626 --> 00:01:36.662
and I am not including Trump's
current lawyer, Rudy Giuliani,

00:01:36.662 --> 00:01:39.732
who we found out Friday is
under federal investigation

00:01:39.732 --> 00:01:41.801
for his links
to Ukrainian energy projects

00:01:41.801 --> 00:01:45.237
or two of Rudy's associates,
Lev and Igor, who were arrested

00:01:45.237 --> 00:01:47.239
in part for their role in this
whole Ukraine scheme.

00:01:47.239 --> 00:01:48.307
Remember these two?

00:01:48.307 --> 00:01:50.243
This looks like a before
and after picture

00:01:50.243 --> 00:01:54.146
except it is before
and even more before.

00:01:54.146 --> 00:01:55.681
They look like
they got their start

00:01:55.681 --> 00:01:59.318
in a live-action game
of Whack-a-Mole.

00:01:59.318 --> 00:02:01.954
They look like they got fired
from their jobs as mall Santas

00:02:01.954 --> 00:02:04.690
for stealing
from the food court.

00:02:04.690 --> 00:02:08.727
[ Russian accent ]
"We thought Auntie Anne's
was free for Santa.

00:02:08.727 --> 00:02:11.063
Why would Auntie charge?"

00:02:11.063 --> 00:02:13.465
[ Normal voice ] In fact,
on Friday, we also found out

00:02:13.465 --> 00:02:15.467
that these two dummies met
privately with Trump

00:02:15.467 --> 00:02:17.303
at the White House,
and that they later told people

00:02:17.303 --> 00:02:19.705
they'd been given a secret
mission by Trump himself.

00:02:19.705 --> 00:02:22.574
-We've learned that both
of the men had a meeting

00:02:22.574 --> 00:02:26.145
with the president and Rudy
Giuliani last year

00:02:26.145 --> 00:02:28.815
at the White House's
annual Hanukkah party

00:02:28.815 --> 00:02:30.783
where they discussed
what Parnas described

00:02:30.783 --> 00:02:33.686
as a secret mission to pressure
the Ukrainian government

00:02:33.686 --> 00:02:35.955
to investigate
former Vice President Joe Biden

00:02:35.955 --> 00:02:37.823
and his son Hunter.

00:02:37.823 --> 00:02:40.193
-Days later we are told that
Parnas insinuated to people

00:02:40.193 --> 00:02:43.062
that he clearly believed he had
been given a special assignment

00:02:43.062 --> 00:02:45.331
by the president, some sort of,
and I'm quoting here,

00:02:45.331 --> 00:02:47.500
"James Bond mission."
-That's right.

00:02:47.500 --> 00:02:51.304
These guys thought they were on
a James Bond mission for Trump.

00:02:51.304 --> 00:02:53.206
I'm sorry,
but these guys aren't 007.

00:02:53.206 --> 00:02:55.375
They're just double Os.

00:02:55.375 --> 00:02:57.877
This is one where I might
believe Trump over them.

00:02:57.877 --> 00:02:59.378
I mean, I can imagine them
cornering Trump

00:02:59.378 --> 00:03:00.646
in a long, boring conversation

00:03:00.646 --> 00:03:02.581
about Van Damme movies
and canned fish,

00:03:02.581 --> 00:03:04.517
and Trump trying to get out of
it by just going,

00:03:04.517 --> 00:03:08.354
[ As Trump ]
"Hey, will you guys go on, like,
a secret mission for me?"

00:03:08.354 --> 00:03:10.056
[ Normal voice ] By the way,
while all this was happening,

00:03:10.056 --> 00:03:11.724
the House was also conducting

00:03:11.724 --> 00:03:13.425
its second day
of public impeachment hearings

00:03:13.425 --> 00:03:16.396
with the former ambassador
to Ukraine, Marie Yovanovitch.

00:03:16.396 --> 00:03:20.266
Basically, Yovanovitch was
the subject of a smear campaign

00:03:20.266 --> 00:03:22.268
by Giuliani and was
abruptly pushed out by Trump

00:03:22.268 --> 00:03:24.003
because they knew
she would be an obstacle

00:03:24.003 --> 00:03:25.471
to their corrupt scheme.

00:03:25.471 --> 00:03:27.339
She is a career foreign-service
officer whose credibility is

00:03:27.339 --> 00:03:28.741
unquestioned by anyone
in either party,

00:03:28.741 --> 00:03:30.243
so, naturally,
as she was testifying,

00:03:30.243 --> 00:03:31.878
Trump decided to attack her.

00:03:31.878 --> 00:03:34.480
-The president attacking former
U.S. Ambassador to Ukraine

00:03:34.480 --> 00:03:37.016
Marie Yovanovitch
during her public testimony

00:03:37.016 --> 00:03:39.452
tweeting, in part,
"Everywhere Marie Yovanovitch

00:03:39.452 --> 00:03:40.919
went turned bad.

00:03:40.919 --> 00:03:44.190
She started off in Somalia.
How did that go?

00:03:44.190 --> 00:03:46.024
Then fast-forward to Ukraine

00:03:46.024 --> 00:03:48.160
where the new Ukrainian
President spoke unfavorably

00:03:48.160 --> 00:03:50.062
about her in my second
phone call with him."

00:03:50.062 --> 00:03:53.732
-Everywhere<i> she</i> went
turned bad?!

00:03:53.732 --> 00:03:56.268
You've gone bankrupt six times
and botched everything

00:03:56.268 --> 00:03:58.838
from casinos to your charity
to your dumb-ass businesses.

00:03:58.838 --> 00:04:01.707
You made a vodka so bad,
no one would drink it.

00:04:01.707 --> 00:04:04.377
Vodka!
How do you screw up vodka?!

00:04:04.377 --> 00:04:05.410
Only Trump.

00:04:05.410 --> 00:04:07.379
[ Laughter, applause ]

00:04:07.379 --> 00:04:10.716
Only Trump could take something

00:04:10.716 --> 00:04:14.386
that's supposed to be flavorless
and make it taste like [bleep].

00:04:14.386 --> 00:04:16.221
But the worst part is
Trump tweeted this

00:04:16.221 --> 00:04:17.656
while she was testifying.

00:04:17.656 --> 00:04:19.725
He tried to intimidate
an impeachment witness

00:04:19.725 --> 00:04:20.826
in real time.

00:04:20.826 --> 00:04:22.261
So, she responded in real time.

00:04:22.261 --> 00:04:23.863
And not only was it
a bad look for Trump,

00:04:23.863 --> 00:04:25.331
but legal analysts
also suggested

00:04:25.331 --> 00:04:26.966
his tweet might have been
a crime.

00:04:26.966 --> 00:04:28.634
-As we sit here testifying,

00:04:28.634 --> 00:04:30.636
the president is attacking you
on Twitter.

00:04:30.636 --> 00:04:33.572
What effect do you think
that has on other witnesses'

00:04:33.572 --> 00:04:38.511
willingness to come forward
and expose wrongdoing?

00:04:38.511 --> 00:04:42.381
-Well, it's very intimidating.

00:04:42.381 --> 00:04:47.753
-It's designed to intimidate,
is it not?

00:04:47.753 --> 00:04:51.724
-I mean, I can't speak to what
the president is trying to do,

00:04:51.724 --> 00:04:54.260
but I think the effect is
to be intimidating.

00:04:54.260 --> 00:04:55.361
-I think there's a good argument

00:04:55.361 --> 00:04:56.629
that given
all the circumstances here,

00:04:56.629 --> 00:04:58.064
given the timing right
in the middle

00:04:58.064 --> 00:05:00.900
of this person's testimony,
given the nature of the tweet,

00:05:00.900 --> 00:05:02.635
that it could be
witness tampering

00:05:02.635 --> 00:05:04.236
or witness retaliation.

00:05:04.236 --> 00:05:06.005
-This could fit
into federal laws

00:05:06.005 --> 00:05:09.976
that are broadly defined
in terms of witness tampering.

00:05:09.976 --> 00:05:12.044
-That's right -- Trump committed
witness tampering

00:05:12.044 --> 00:05:13.946
during an impeachment hearing.

00:05:13.946 --> 00:05:17.283
That's like punching the bailiff
during your assault trial.

00:05:17.283 --> 00:05:18.817
[ Laughter ]

00:05:18.817 --> 00:05:20.252
But I think I know
what he's doing here.

00:05:20.252 --> 00:05:22.155
You see, Trump figures
if he just keeps committing

00:05:22.155 --> 00:05:24.357
impeachable offenses, Democrats
will have to keep investigating

00:05:24.357 --> 00:05:26.325
those offenses
which means they'll never

00:05:26.325 --> 00:05:28.060
actually have time
to impeach him.

00:05:28.060 --> 00:05:29.828
He thinks he can just keep
committing crimes

00:05:29.828 --> 00:05:31.297
to run out the clock.

00:05:31.297 --> 00:05:33.232
At the next hearing, he's going
to drop in from the ceiling

00:05:33.232 --> 00:05:35.134
and steal everyone's wallets
like Tom Cruise

00:05:35.134 --> 00:05:37.402
in "Mission Impossible."

00:05:37.402 --> 00:05:41.173
In fact, this was so bad
that even Fox News had to admit

00:05:41.173 --> 00:05:43.009
when it happened that Trump
had only strengthened

00:05:43.009 --> 00:05:44.543
the impeachment case
against him.

00:05:44.543 --> 00:05:47.046
-The president was not advised
by counsel

00:05:47.046 --> 00:05:49.915
in deciding to do this tweet.

00:05:49.915 --> 00:05:52.719
Extraordinarily poor judgment.

00:05:52.719 --> 00:05:54.520
-And that does raise
the possibility

00:05:54.520 --> 00:05:57.155
of witness intimidation
and witness tampering

00:05:57.155 --> 00:05:58.858
as a new charge here.

00:05:58.858 --> 00:06:01.193
-This whole hearing
turned on a dime

00:06:01.193 --> 00:06:04.663
when the president tweeted
about her real time.

00:06:04.663 --> 00:06:08.334
Now, that enabled Schiff
to then characterize that tweet

00:06:08.334 --> 00:06:11.337
as intimidating the witness
or tampering with the witness,

00:06:11.337 --> 00:06:13.238
which is a crime,

00:06:13.238 --> 00:06:17.243
adding essentially an article
of impeachment real time.

00:06:17.243 --> 00:06:18.911
-That's right.
Trump added

00:06:18.911 --> 00:06:21.079
another article of impeachment
in real time.

00:06:21.079 --> 00:06:22.949
At this point he should just
start doing

00:06:22.949 --> 00:06:25.651
DVD director's commentary
during the hearings.

00:06:25.651 --> 00:06:28.120
-[ As Trump ] "As you can see
here, that's Marie Yovanovitch.

00:06:28.120 --> 00:06:30.889
I pushed her out so I could
bribe the president of Ukraine.

00:06:30.889 --> 00:06:32.792
That was a fun scene.

00:06:32.792 --> 00:06:34.259
And, oh, here's Jim Jordan.

00:06:34.259 --> 00:06:38.097
We pulled a prank on set
where we stole Jim's jacket."

00:06:38.097 --> 00:06:40.832
[ Normal voice ] Still,
if you're Republican, I get it.

00:06:40.832 --> 00:06:42.534
It's just so hard to say.

00:06:42.534 --> 00:06:43.936
Is Trump innocent,
or is he guilty?

00:06:43.936 --> 00:06:45.972
I mean, all we have so far is

00:06:45.972 --> 00:06:47.673
the six Trump associates
convicted of a crime,

00:06:47.673 --> 00:06:48.807
two more indicted associates

00:06:48.807 --> 00:06:50.342
saying they were
on a secret mission for him,

00:06:50.342 --> 00:06:51.944
his lawyer
under criminal investigation,

00:06:51.944 --> 00:06:53.446
Trump himself committing
witness tampering,

00:06:53.446 --> 00:06:54.780
the whistle-blower's account

00:06:54.780 --> 00:06:56.115
claiming the president clearly
committed a criminal act,

00:06:56.115 --> 00:06:57.683
the notes from the call,
in which Trump mentions

00:06:57.683 --> 00:06:59.418
the Bidens multiple times,
the part of the call

00:06:59.418 --> 00:07:00.853
where Trump tells
the Ukrainian President

00:07:00.853 --> 00:07:02.154
"I would like you
to do us a favor,"

00:07:02.154 --> 00:07:03.455
the president's chief of staff

00:07:03.455 --> 00:07:05.123
literally confessing
on national television,

00:07:05.123 --> 00:07:06.492
Rudy Giuliani going on TV

00:07:06.492 --> 00:07:07.726
and bragging about
what he was doing,

00:07:07.726 --> 00:07:08.961
and, like,
a bunch of witnesses saying,

00:07:08.961 --> 00:07:11.130
"Yes, there was a quid pro quo."
I'm sorry!

00:07:11.130 --> 00:07:13.432
That's not enough to convict!

00:07:13.432 --> 00:07:15.468
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:07:17.703 --> 00:07:21.140
-Republicans won't budge

00:07:21.140 --> 00:07:23.609
unless we have a photo
of Trump on the phone

00:07:23.609 --> 00:07:25.877
with a word bubble coming
out of his mouth saying,

00:07:25.877 --> 00:07:29.048
"I am doing a crime now."

00:07:29.048 --> 00:07:30.949
I mean, just take
that quote where Trump told

00:07:30.949 --> 00:07:32.084
the president of Ukraine,

00:07:32.084 --> 00:07:33.518
"I would like you to do us
a favor."

00:07:33.518 --> 00:07:35.688
We just have no way of knowing
what he really meant.

00:07:35.688 --> 00:07:38.191
It's not like Trump has said
himself on camera

00:07:38.191 --> 00:07:39.658
for the entire world to see

00:07:39.658 --> 00:07:40.927
that he wanted
the president of Ukraine

00:07:40.927 --> 00:07:42.928
to start a major investigation
into the Bidens.

00:07:42.928 --> 00:07:45.864
-What exactly did you hope
Zelensky would do

00:07:45.864 --> 00:07:48.000
about the Bidens
after your phone call?

00:07:48.000 --> 00:07:51.970
-Well, I would think that if
they were honest about it,

00:07:51.970 --> 00:07:54.973
they'd start a major
investigation into the Bidens.

00:07:54.973 --> 00:07:57.643
It's a very simple answer.

00:07:57.643 --> 00:08:00.112
They should investigate
the Bidens.

00:08:00.112 --> 00:08:04.350
-Damn it, Donald!
Why are you so coy?!

00:08:04.350 --> 00:08:06.285
But in case you still needed
more evidence

00:08:06.285 --> 00:08:08.087
tying Trump directly
to the scheme

00:08:08.087 --> 00:08:09.221
to extort a foreign country

00:08:09.221 --> 00:08:10.756
to investigate
his political rivals

00:08:10.756 --> 00:08:12.524
by dangling hundreds
of millions of dollars

00:08:12.524 --> 00:08:14.493
in taxpayer money,
you got that evidence

00:08:14.493 --> 00:08:16.061
from last week's
impeachment hearings.

00:08:16.061 --> 00:08:18.898
Multiple witnesses tied Trump
and his lawyer, Rudy Giuliani,

00:08:18.898 --> 00:08:20.966
directly to the quid pro quo,
and one witness,

00:08:20.966 --> 00:08:22.935
Ambassador Bill Taylor,
even revealed

00:08:22.935 --> 00:08:26.172
some bombshell new information
about a phone call Trump had had

00:08:26.172 --> 00:08:28.741
with one of his key henchmen,
the Ambassador to the E.U.,

00:08:28.741 --> 00:08:30.009
Gordon Sondland.

00:08:30.009 --> 00:08:33.012
-Taylor said a staffer of his
recently told him

00:08:33.012 --> 00:08:35.948
about this conversation
involving the president

00:08:35.948 --> 00:08:39.452
and the Trump donor
turned ambassador to the E.U.,

00:08:39.452 --> 00:08:40.919
Gordon Sondland.

00:08:40.919 --> 00:08:43.122
-In the presence of my staff
at a restaurant,

00:08:43.122 --> 00:08:45.458
Ambassador Sondland
called President Trump

00:08:45.458 --> 00:08:49.361
and told him of his meetings
in Kiev.

00:08:49.361 --> 00:08:51.230
The member of my staff
could hear President Trump

00:08:51.230 --> 00:08:53.431
on the phone
asking Ambassador Sondland

00:08:53.431 --> 00:08:55.434
about the investigations.

00:08:55.434 --> 00:08:57.803
-This was a cellphone I take it?
-It was a cellphone.

00:08:57.803 --> 00:08:59.338
-The president must have been
speaking loud enough

00:08:59.338 --> 00:09:02.441
for your staff member
to be able to overhear this?

00:09:02.441 --> 00:09:04.377
-He was.

00:09:04.377 --> 00:09:06.078
-These guys are such morons.

00:09:06.078 --> 00:09:08.147
Trump was in the process
of committing a crime,

00:09:08.147 --> 00:09:10.516
and he was screaming
into the phone so loudly,

00:09:10.516 --> 00:09:13.219
everyone on the other end
could hear him.

00:09:13.219 --> 00:09:14.686
That's what happens
when you're used to doing

00:09:14.686 --> 00:09:16.155
all your press conferences
outside

00:09:16.155 --> 00:09:18.924
next to a giant helicopter.

00:09:18.924 --> 00:09:20.993
It's like taking a date
to a Metallica concert.

00:09:20.993 --> 00:09:23.128
[ Shouting ] "I'm having
a really great time tonight!"

00:09:23.128 --> 00:09:24.964
"What?!"

00:09:24.964 --> 00:09:27.966
"I said I'm having
a really great time tonight!"

00:09:27.966 --> 00:09:32.338
"Did you say you'd like
to commit a crime tonight?"

00:09:32.338 --> 00:09:34.473
"Yeah!"

00:09:34.473 --> 00:09:36.742
[ Normal voice ]
Trump yelled so loud,
everyone could hear him.

00:09:36.742 --> 00:09:38.110
Honestly,
it would have been easier

00:09:38.110 --> 00:09:39.678
if Trump had just held
a conference call

00:09:39.678 --> 00:09:41.513
and let everyone dial in.

00:09:41.513 --> 00:09:44.316
<i> -President Trump has joined
 the conference call.</i>

00:09:44.316 --> 00:09:47.019
-Hello, everybody. Thank you
very much for being here.

00:09:47.019 --> 00:09:49.455
Ukraine --
To investigate the Bidens.

00:09:49.455 --> 00:09:50.622
And I'm -- guilty.

00:09:50.622 --> 00:09:52.925
<i> -This conference call
 has ended.</i>

00:09:52.925 --> 00:09:55.460
-So, a witness
literally overheard Trump

00:09:55.460 --> 00:09:56.929
yelling about his crime
on a phone call

00:09:56.929 --> 00:09:58.230
with one of his key henchmen.

00:09:58.230 --> 00:10:00.132
And just in case it wasn't
already incredibly clear

00:10:00.132 --> 00:10:01.533
what had happened on that call,

00:10:01.533 --> 00:10:04.136
we found out on Friday from that
witness what happened next.

00:10:04.136 --> 00:10:06.572
The witness, a State Department
official named David Holmes,

00:10:06.572 --> 00:10:08.807
testified that after Sondland
hung up with Trump,

00:10:08.807 --> 00:10:11.577
he basically admitted everything
on the spot.

00:10:11.577 --> 00:10:13.645
-Following the call
with President Trump,

00:10:13.645 --> 00:10:15.948
the member of my staff
asked Ambassador Sondland

00:10:15.948 --> 00:10:18.250
what President Trump thought
about Ukraine.

00:10:18.250 --> 00:10:20.952
Ambassador Sondland responded
that President Trump

00:10:20.952 --> 00:10:23.556
cares more about
the investigations of Biden,

00:10:23.556 --> 00:10:25.657
which Giuliani was pressing for.

00:10:25.657 --> 00:10:30.662
-I want to a read section
from Holmes' sworn testimony,

00:10:30.662 --> 00:10:31.997
his opening statement.

00:10:31.997 --> 00:10:33.799
"In particular,
I asked Ambassador Sondland,"

00:10:33.799 --> 00:10:35.200
this is David Holmes speaking,

00:10:35.200 --> 00:10:38.337
"if it true that the president
did not give a [bleep]" --

00:10:38.337 --> 00:10:40.239
excuse the language --
"about Ukraine.

00:10:40.239 --> 00:10:42.074
Ambassador Sondland agreed
that the president

00:10:42.074 --> 00:10:44.409
did not give a [bleep]
about Ukraine."

00:10:44.409 --> 00:10:45.945
-He literally hung up the phone

00:10:45.945 --> 00:10:47.680
and said Trump doesn't give
a [bleep] about Ukraine.

00:10:47.680 --> 00:10:49.381
He only cares about
investigating the Bidens.

00:10:49.381 --> 00:10:50.549
He just admitted it.

00:10:50.549 --> 00:10:52.150
It's like if you saw your spouse
on their phone

00:10:52.150 --> 00:10:53.352
and said,
"Are you texting a friend?"

00:10:53.352 --> 00:10:55.320
and they said, "Honey,
she's more than a friend.

00:10:55.320 --> 00:10:56.789
She's my mistress."

00:10:56.789 --> 00:11:00.593
[ Laughter ]

00:11:00.593 --> 00:11:03.195
So, Friday's deposition could
not have made it any more clear.

00:11:03.195 --> 00:11:05.497
Not only did Trump try to extort
the president of Ukraine

00:11:05.497 --> 00:11:07.700
during his own phone call with
that country's president,

00:11:07.700 --> 00:11:10.368
Trump was also calling
other key players in the scheme

00:11:10.368 --> 00:11:12.104
and checking in with them, too.

00:11:12.104 --> 00:11:14.339
In fact during his deposition
on Friday, Holmes also said

00:11:14.339 --> 00:11:16.575
that he overheard Sondland
and Trump discussing

00:11:16.575 --> 00:11:17.976
the pressure campaign directed

00:11:17.976 --> 00:11:20.479
toward Ukrainian President
Zelensky and what he heard was

00:11:20.479 --> 00:11:22.848
both very colorful
and very damning.

00:11:22.848 --> 00:11:25.184
-"I heard Ambassador Sondland
greet the president

00:11:25.184 --> 00:11:28.521
and explain that he was calling
from Kiev.

00:11:28.521 --> 00:11:31.523
I heard President Trump
then clarify

00:11:31.523 --> 00:11:34.059
that Ambassador Sondland was
in Ukraine.

00:11:34.059 --> 00:11:36.595
Ambassador Sondland replied,
Yes, he was in Ukraine,

00:11:36.595 --> 00:11:39.665
and went on to state
that President Zelensky

00:11:39.665 --> 00:11:41.867
"loves your ass."

00:11:41.867 --> 00:11:43.402
-That's right Trump's henchman

00:11:43.402 --> 00:11:45.337
actually told him,
"Zelensky loves your ass."

00:11:45.337 --> 00:11:46.939
I mean, it's
classic bad-guy talk.

00:11:46.939 --> 00:11:49.107
That's something the
wolf of wall street would say

00:11:49.107 --> 00:11:50.976
after snorting cocaine
off a stripper's butt.

00:11:50.976 --> 00:11:54.112
"Whoo! Daddy loves your ass!"

00:11:54.112 --> 00:11:58.116
Now, Trump has denied ever
taking the call from Sondland

00:11:58.116 --> 00:12:00.218
despite the fact that
we now have multiple witnesses

00:12:00.218 --> 00:12:02.387
confirming it, although,
it's clear from his denial

00:12:02.387 --> 00:12:04.456
that Trump was,
as always, lying.

00:12:04.456 --> 00:12:08.360
-There was one moment where
Ambassador Bill Taylor recounted

00:12:08.360 --> 00:12:11.964
a conversation
that an aide of his overheard

00:12:11.964 --> 00:12:14.199
in which the aide says
that he overheard you

00:12:14.199 --> 00:12:17.769
say to Sondland,
"How are things proceeding

00:12:17.769 --> 00:12:19.605
with the investigations?"

00:12:19.605 --> 00:12:22.074
Is that correct,
and can you fill in some more?

00:12:22.074 --> 00:12:24.076
-I know nothing about that.
First time I've heard it.

00:12:24.076 --> 00:12:25.778
-Do you recall a conversation --

00:12:25.778 --> 00:12:27.346
-I don't recall. No.
Not at all.

00:12:27.346 --> 00:12:29.047
-Yeah but you do.

00:12:29.047 --> 00:12:31.850
Any time Trump says he doesn't
recall, he definitely recalls.

00:12:31.850 --> 00:12:33.118
He always does this.

00:12:33.118 --> 00:12:35.187
You can show flash cards
of the people closest to him

00:12:35.187 --> 00:12:37.022
in his life, and he'd pretend
he doesn't recognize them.

00:12:37.022 --> 00:12:38.623
-[ As Trump ] "What?
No, never met him.

00:12:38.623 --> 00:12:40.425
Doesn't look familiar.

00:12:40.425 --> 00:12:43.329
Is he an extra
in 'The Walking Dead?'"

00:12:43.329 --> 00:12:45.331
[ Laughter ]

00:12:45.331 --> 00:12:46.464
-"I don't know."

00:12:46.464 --> 00:12:47.933
-[ Normal voice ]
Trump has pulled this move

00:12:47.933 --> 00:12:50.269
so many times, and every time,
we found out that he's lying.

00:12:50.269 --> 00:12:52.070
Remember
when the news first broke

00:12:52.070 --> 00:12:54.205
that his lawyer Michael Cohen
had illegally paid off

00:12:54.205 --> 00:12:56.375
Stormy Daniels to cover up
Trump's affair with her?

00:12:56.375 --> 00:12:57.743
Trump denied
knowing anything about it,

00:12:57.743 --> 00:12:59.578
but we later found out
that Trump had reimbursed Cohen

00:12:59.578 --> 00:13:01.146
and orchestrated
the whole thing.

00:13:01.146 --> 00:13:03.081
In fact, we literally saw
a copy of the check

00:13:03.081 --> 00:13:04.583
Trump wrote to Cohen.

00:13:04.583 --> 00:13:06.618
And you can tell it's Trump's
signature because it looks like

00:13:06.618 --> 00:13:10.789
he was trying to draw a straight
line while riding a seesaw.

00:13:10.789 --> 00:13:13.292
We already have all the evidence
we can possibly need,

00:13:13.292 --> 00:13:15.995
and there's still more witnesses
waiting to testify.

00:13:15.995 --> 00:13:17.563
Republicans have no defense.

00:13:17.563 --> 00:13:18.898
All they can do
during these hearings

00:13:18.898 --> 00:13:21.199
is perform for Trump
to earn his approval.

00:13:21.199 --> 00:13:22.767
I wouldn't be surprised
if at some point this week,

00:13:22.767 --> 00:13:24.936
a GOP congressman looked
directly into the camera

00:13:24.936 --> 00:13:27.406
and said, "President Trump,
the Republican Party --

00:13:27.406 --> 00:13:29.007
-Loves your ass.

00:13:29.007 --> 00:13:31.143
-This has been "A Closer Look."

00:13:31.143 --> 00:13:33.913
[ Cheers and applause ]

